	(descr "The network module's bay on a host board, with the module link's socket (boards/contracts/module-link.md v3 sections 7 and 10, 2026-11-19): the module (network-module-stm32h743, 56.31 x 57.59 mm) stands over it on four M3 standoffs (11.0 mm), its 2 x 20 header plugged into the 2 x 20 2.54 mm socket strip here (pads 1-40, through-hole, drawn reference Samtec SSW-120-01-G-D, body 8.51 mm) at exactly the place the header lands. Four NPTH 3.2 mm holes at the module's corner-hole pattern (46.16 x 47.44 mm) with the 8.4 mm copper keep-out, and the chimney: 32 NPTH 5.0 mm vent holes clear of the socket. No other host part under the module (traces and planes may run under it). Courtyard = the module's outline + 0.5 mm. F.Fab: the module unturned, its north edge (RJ45) the -y side. A host turns the bay by its netlist's mating_side. STAGED for the owner to install.")
